<title>USA: Dataram board approves repurchase plan.</title>
<headline>Dataram board approves repurchase plan.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dataram Corp's Chief Executive Robert Tarantino said Friday its directors approved the buyback of 300,000 shares, or about 10 percent of the common stock.</p>
<p>The company said in a press release the shares may be repurchased from time to time either on the American Stock Exchange or through block purchases.</p>
<p>Dataram Corp is a developer, maker and marketer of gigabyte memory upgrades for UNIX and Windows/NT workstations and servers.</p>
</text>
